{
  "_about": "Shared glossary + per-language style for tools/i18n-sync.js. 'keep' = never translated. 'terms' = how the site's own words are already translated: each term's 'from' key is read from every catalog by `node tools/i18n-sync.js --glossary` (it refreshes 'tr'). Edit 'note' / 'style' by hand; a human-fixed term can set 'locked': true to stop the refresh.",
  "keep": [
    "PATV",
    "PAT",
    "Pepe",
    "PepeFrog",
    "Public Access TV",
    "Camfrog",
    "Prime Time",
    "Season Pass",
    "Grand Theft Frogger",
    "Fort Knox",
    "Discord",
    "Twitch",
    "YouTube",
    "Plex",
    "Overseerr",
    "Wizarr",
    "Spotify",
    "Texas Hold'em",
    "Blackjack",
    "PepeLab"
  ],
  "rules": [
    "Casual, friendly, short: this is a community site (live video rooms, chat games, a points economy), not a bank.",
    "Brand and product names in 'keep' stay exactly as written, in Latin script.",
    "Chat commands (!wallet, !avatar regen, @name, p/name) and anything in <code> stay as they are.",
    "PAT is the site's points currency: write amounts like '20,000 PAT' with the language's own digit grouping but keep 'PAT'.",
    "A 'pad' is a community space (like a subreddit with a live stage); a 'stage' is a pad's live video slot. Use the glossary words.",
    "UI labels (buttons, tabs, menu items) stay short; do not add punctuation English doesn't have."
  ],
